messages:
maya: Quick check — opened a Terraform PR to tweak HPA target utilization (60 -> 50) for the inference pool and add conservative Karpenter provisioner min/max constraints. Can someone do a quick sanity review? PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/infra/pull/452
sam: pinging @oliver for Karpenter/scale policy eyes
maya: pasted the HPA block in the PR but here it is inline too:
```hcl
resource \"kubernetes_horizontal_pod_autoscaler_v2\" \"inference\" {
  metadata { name = \"inference-hpa\" namespace = \"inference\" }
  spec {
    scale_target_ref { api_version = \"apps/v1\" kind = \"Deployment\" name = \"inference-depl\" }
    min_replicas = 1
    max_replicas = 12
    metrics {
      type = \"Resource\"
      resource { name = \"cpu\" target { type = \"Utilization\" average_utilization = 50 } }
    }
    behavior {
      scale_up { stabilization_window_seconds = 30 }
      scale_down { stabilization_window_seconds = 60 }
    }
  }
}
```
oliver: skimmed the TF plan — two notes:
1) For prod we should raise min_replicas -> 2 to avoid cold start latency on tails. staging can stay at 1.
2) On the Karpenter provisioner, add `ttlSecondsUntilExpired = 300` and a soft `consolidation = false` toggle until we validate consolidation impact on latency. Also add a max node lifetime so we don't churn too much when we roll kernels.
sam: question: where are we wiring the metrics adapter secret? earlier changes moved vault paths around and the vpa/metrics adapter needs `secret/data/metrics/adapter`. Did PR update helm values?
infra-bot: Terraform plan completed for branch maya/hpa-tune — no drift, 1 change(s) to apply. Plan URL: https://ci.redwood/terraform/plan/789
kevin: about VPA interaction — lowering HPA target util could fight with VPA recommended CPU. To reduce oscillation I suggest explicitly setting `stabilizationWindowSeconds` (down) to 60 and `tolerance` on the VPA (or use mode: \"Auto\" but with updateMode: \"Off\" for the first canary).
tia: also, PLEASE ensure liveness/readiness probe timeouts are sane. We saw probe-triggered restarts during last scale test. Maybe increase readiness initialDelaySeconds to 15 for now and have probe timeout 5s.
maya: good catches — I'll: 1) set min_replicas=2 for prod, leave staging=1, 2) add ttlSecondsUntilExpired and consolidation toggle in provisioner TF, 3) add stabilizationWindowSeconds = 60 to scale_down, 4) bump readiness probe initialDelay for the deployment, 5) update Helm chart secret path to `secret/data/metrics/adapter`.
sam: I can own the charts PR for the metrics path change, will open it today and include a helm values diff.
oliver: once sam's chart change is in, let's run a small canary: staging with 3 replicas, exercise a synthetic load, watch node churn + HPA/VPA signals. If metrics look noisy, enable VPA updateMode: Off and retest.
maya: noted. I'll add a checklist in the infra PR description: helm chart PR, canary staging run, validate probes/eviction behavior, merge TF after green canary.
kevin: minor nit — annotate the deployment with `autoscaling.alpha.kubernetes.io/avoid-rollout: \"true\"` during the canary so Karpenter/cluster autoscaler doesn't cause an immediate rollout when nodes change.
tia: +1 :thumbsup:
maya: thanks all. I updated the PR description with the checklist and changed the prod min_replicas note. Marking this thread resolved for now — will post results after the staging canary. :white_check_mark:
